  "title": "Spot the Easy Shortcut",
  "description": "When making a quick judgment: - Ask yourself: \"Am I replacing a complex decision with an easy shortcut?\" - Check for oversimplification: Write down what factors you might be ignoring. - Verify with evidence: Compare the easy answer to what the data or context actually suggests. Example: Choosing a restaurant based solely on star ratings might ignore crucial factors like location or budget.",
